cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Please also cite the underlying Elam atomic data; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md."
title: "X-ray Attenuation Workbench for Multicomponent Materials and Multilayers"
version: "1.0.0"
type: software
license: MIT
# First stable release. It supersedes the 0.1.x calculator, whose original
# citation is preserved in legacy/CITATION.cff, and whose multicomponent script
# double-weighted mass fractions. Before publishing, replace the DOI below with
# the Zenodo *concept* DOI ("Cite all versions") so citations aggregate across
# releases rather than pinning to one, and set date-released to the release day.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.17602371
authors:
  - family-names: Jalaludeen
    given-names: Mohamed Faizal Ussama
repository-code: "https://github.com/faizalusama/X-ray_attenuation_calculator"
abstract: >-
  A local graphical and programmable workbench for narrow-beam X-ray
  attenuation in multicomponent materials and planar multilayers.
  This development version has not been published as a new release.
